cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sindhi-Jev, please cite it as below. A paper is in preparation."
title: "Sindhi-Jev: a small dot-aware checker for Sindhi OCR"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kaleem
    given-names: Arsalan
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Shikarpur, Sindh, Pakistan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9054-6965"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArsalanKaleem/sindhi-JEV"
url: "https://arsalankaleem.me/sindhi-JEV/"
keywords:
  - Sindhi
  - OCR
  - OCR error detection
  - Arabic script
  - low-resource languages
abstract: >-
  A 7M-parameter render-and-verify model that checks whether Sindhi OCR text
  matches a scanned word crop and flags letters with dot errors, with a frozen,
  hand-labelled real benchmark (336 word crops from 14 printed sources).
  AUROC 0.884 overall and 0.935 on dot errors on that benchmark.
